# This repository (code-guardian) is checked out at the agent's HOME root
# (/home/agent), which also contains secrets and runtime state (.ssh, .claude,
# .config, work/, ...). To make `git add -A` safe and never capture those,
# ignore EVERYTHING at the top level by default, then re-include only the
# agent-definition files this repo actually tracks.
#
# NOTE: NOTHING under work/ is tracked — it is all runtime state, seeded on a
# fresh volume from the templates in ONBOARDING.md (Step 3b), not from this repo.
# The `/*` rule hides every untracked top-level path (HOME secrets, all of work/,
# an inner work/.git, ...); only the definition files re-included below are
# versioned. This keeps `git add -A` at $HOME safe and lets a deployed instance
# update the definition (`git reset --hard origin/main`) without ever colliding
# with its live work/ state.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/ONBOARDING.md
!/LICENSE
!/docs/
!/scripts/

# Never track these even if a future allowlist entry would pull them in.
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
